<header><p class="st-kicker">colony · Central and Southern Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">British Bechuanaland</h1><p class="st-meta">1885 CE – 1895 CE · capital Vryburg</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The British Crown colony south of the Molopo River, created in 1885 to secure the road to the interior.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warren-expedition">Warren Expedition</a> dispersed the freebooter republics of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/stellaland">Stellaland</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/goshen">Goshen</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> proclaimed southern <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/bechuanaland-protectorate">Bechuanaland</a>, between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/molopo-river">Molopo River</a> and the Cape border, a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crown-colony">Crown colony</a> on 30 September 1885, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vryburg">Vryburg</a> as its capital.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>An administrator, Sir <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sidney-shippard">Sidney Shippard</a>, governed the colony, which included the lands of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/batlhaping-chiefdom">Tlhaping</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barolong">Barolong</a>. Much land was allocated to white farmers, while reserves were set aside for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tswana-people">Tswana</a> chiefs such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/montshiwa">Montshiwa</a>. The colony secured the route along which the railway to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahikeng">Mafeking</a> was later built.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>British <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/bechuanaland-protectorate">Bechuanaland</a> was annexed to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/cape-colony">Cape Colony</a> in 1895 and later became part of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-south-africa">South Africa</a>. The territory north of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/molopo-river">Molopo</a> remained the Bechuanaland <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">Protectorate</a>, which became independent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/botswana">Botswana</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/british-bechuanaland.jpg" alt="British Bechuanaland" width="320" height="192"><figcaption>Image: Original: Acts of Union 1800 Vector: Yaddah · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_United_Kingdom_(3-5).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1885 CE – 1895 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>colony</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Vryburg</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Sidney Shippard</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Christianity, Tswana traditional religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Setswana, English, Dutch</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/south-africa">South Africa</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Crown Colony of British Bechuanaland</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1890&amp;focus=british-bechuanaland" aria-label="British Bechuanaland on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5331 3167 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where British Bechuanaland lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5651 3423L4997 651M5651 3423L5651 3423M5651 3423L5682 3386M5651 3423L5470 3663M5651 3423L5628 3427"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4997 651h0M5651 3423h0M5682 3386h0M5470 3663h0M5628 3427h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5651 3423h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5651 3423h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Vryburg. <a href="/atlas?year=1890&amp;focus=british-bechuanaland">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
